      <description>&lt;style&gt;&#xA;.prose .ps-page { max-width: none; }&#xA;.prose .ps-page *:where(:not(.ps-value a)) { margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; }&#xA;.ps-page { font-family: Inter, &#34;Segoe UI&#34;, &#34;PingFang SC&#34;, &#34;Microsoft YaHei&#34;, sans-serif; color: #0a1d37; }&#xA;.ps-page * { box-sizing: border-box; }&#xA;.ps-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e8ecf0; border-radius: 10px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(10, 29, 55, 0.04); }&#xA;.ps-section-title { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0a1d37; margin: 0 0 16px; }&#xA;.ps-divider { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #eef1f5; margin: 16px 0; }&#xA;.ps-centered-header { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 12px; margin: 8px 0 24px; color: #0a1d37; font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; }&#xA;.ps-centered-header::before, .ps-centered-header::after { content: &#34;&#34;; flex: 1; height: 1px; background: #dbe2ea; max-width: 200px; }&#xA;.ps-profile { display: block; }&#xA;.ps-profile-name { font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 16px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding-bottom: 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eef1f5; }&#xA;.ps-info-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0; }&#xA;.ps-info-item { padding: 14px 20px 14px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #eef1f5; }&#xA;.ps-info-item:nth-child(even) { padding-left: 20px; padding-right: 0; border-left: 1px solid #eef1f5; }&#xA;.ps-label { font-size: 12px; color: #8b95a5; margin-bottom: 4px; }&#xA;.ps-value { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #0a1d37; }&#xA;.ps-value a { color: #2563eb; text-decoration: none; }&#xA;.ps-bio { font-size: 14px; color: #5c6b7a; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 16px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid #eef1f5; }&#xA;.ps-product-name { background: #f0f4f8; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #0a1d37; }&#xA;.ps-product-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; background: #f0f4f8; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; }&#xA;.ps-product-info { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; }&#xA;.ps-product-thumb { width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 6px; object-fit: contain; background: #fff; }&#xA;.ps-btn-group { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }&#xA;.ps-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; padding: 8px 14px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; border: 1px solid #dbe2ea; background: #fff; color: #0a1d37; text-decoration: none; }&#xA;.ps-btn-primary { background: #2563eb; border-color: #2563eb; color: #fff; }&#xA;.ps-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }&#xA;.ps-grid.cols-2 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }&#xA;.ps-grid-item { padding: 16px 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eef1f5; }&#xA;.ps-grid-item .ps-value { font-size: 17px; }&#xA;.ps-subsection { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0a1d37; margin: 8px 0 0; padding: 8px 20px 0; }&#xA;.ps-code { background: #f3f5f8; border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 16px; font-family: Consolas, &#34;Courier New&#34;, monospace; font-size: 13px; color: #334155; word-break: break-all; margin-top: 12px; }&#xA;.ps-card-actions { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-left: auto; }&#xA;.ps-btn-sm { padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 12px; }&#xA;.ps-crosshair-carousel { position: relative; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 0 0 16px; background: #111; aspect-ratio: 909 / 160; }&#xA;.ps-crosshair-track { display: flex; height: 100%; transition: transform 0.35s ease; }&#xA;.ps-crosshair-slide { flex: 0 0 100%; height: 100%; }&#xA;.ps-crosshair-slide img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }&#xA;.ps-crosshair-overlay { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); pointer-events: none; z-index: 2; }&#xA;.ps-crosshair-arrow { position: absolute; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%); z-index: 3; width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 50%; border: none; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.75); color: #0a1d37; cursor: pointer; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 22px; line-height: 1; padding: 0; transition: background 0.15s; }&#xA;.ps-crosshair-arrow:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.95); }&#xA;.ps-crosshair-arrow--prev { left: 12px; }&#xA;.ps-crosshair-arrow--next { right: 12px; }&#xA;.ps-crosshair-dots { position: absolute; bottom: 10px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); z-index: 3; display: flex; gap: 6px; }&#xA;.ps-crosshair-dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; border: none; padding: 0; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.45); cursor: pointer; }&#xA;.ps-crosshair-dot.active { background: #fff; }&#xA;.ps-gear-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 16px; }&#xA;.ps-gear-card { background: #f3f5f8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px; position: relative; min-height: 140px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }&#xA;.ps-gear-badge { position: absolute; top: 10px; right: 10px; background: #0a1d37; color: #fff; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 4px; }&#xA;.ps-gear-img { max-width: 100%; max-height: 100px; object-fit: contain; }&#xA;.ps-gear-name { font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; margin-top: 10px; color: #0a1d37; }&#xA;.ps-gear-sub { font-size: 13px; color: #5c6b7a; font-weight: 400; }&#xA;.ps-hw-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 16px; }&#xA;.ps-hw-card { background: #f3f5f8; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; }&#xA;.ps-hw-img-wrap { padding: 20px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 160px; position: relative; }&#xA;.ps-hw-name { padding: 12px 16px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; }&#xA;.ps-skins-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 16px; }&#xA;.ps-skin-card { background: #f3f5f8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px; position: relative; min-height: 120px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; overflow: hidden; }&#xA;.ps-skin-card .ps-gear-img { background: #1a1a1a; border-radius: 6px; padding: 8px; max-height: 90px; }&#xA;.ps-gear-card .ps-gear-img { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-height: 90px; }&#xA;.ps-skin-name { font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; margin-top: 10px; line-height: 1.4; }&#xA;@media (max-width: 768px) {&#xA;  .ps-info-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }&#xA;  .ps-info-item:nth-child(even) { padding-left: 0; border-left: 0; }&#xA;  .ps-grid, .ps-gear-grid, .ps-skins-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }&#xA;  .ps-hw-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/style&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;ps-page not-prose&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;ps-card&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;ps-profile&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h2 class=&#34;ps-profile-name&#34;&gt;donk &lt;span style=&#34;font-size:14px;color:#8b95a5;font-weight:400;&#34;&gt;ⓘ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;ps-info-grid&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;div class=&#34;ps-info-item&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;ps-label&#34;&gt;战队&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;ps-value&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#&#34;&gt;Team Spirit&lt;/a&gt; 🐉&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;      &lt;div class=&#34;ps-info-item&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;ps-label&#34;&gt;国籍&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;ps-value&#34;&gt;俄罗斯 🇷🇺&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;      &lt;div class=&#34;ps-info-item&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;ps-label&#34;&gt;姓名&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;ps-value&#34;&gt;Danil Kryshkovets&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;      &lt;div class=&#34;ps-info-item&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;ps-label&#34;&gt;生日&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;ps-value&#34;&gt;2007 年 1 月 25 日&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;p class=&#34;ps-bio&#34;&gt;Danil「donk」Kryshkovets 是一名职业《反恐精英 2》选手，目前效力于 Team Spirit，司职步枪手（Rifler）。&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>CS2 R8 Revolver: The Anti-Human Charging &#39;Wheelchair God&#39;</title>
      <link>https://acebase.cc/posts/cs2-r8-revolver-the-anti-human-charging-god-of-wheelchairs-en/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 03 Jun 2026 10:00:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://acebase.cc/posts/cs2-r8-revolver-the-anti-human-charging-god-of-wheelchairs-en/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;cs2-r8-revolver-the-anti-human-charging-wheelchair-god&#34;&gt;CS2 R8 Revolver: The Anti-Human Charging &amp;quot;Wheelchair God&amp;quot;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Introduction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;You think mashing the left mouse button fires the gun? In CS2, the R8 Revolver refuses to let you do that — it stubbornly turns &amp;quot;pulling the trigger&amp;quot; into a calculus problem: hold for 0.2 seconds to charge, applies a movement speed debuff, and even has an audible &amp;quot;countdown broadcast&amp;quot; before firing... But it&#39;s precisely this seemingly anti-human design that makes it a three-in-one tool: an eco-round comeback nuke, a wallbang assassin, and a psychological warfare master. Today, we tear open the mystery of this $600 &amp;quot;budget sniper,&amp;quot; from its three counter-intuitive features and two unique techniques, to the hidden full-auto easter egg that 99% of players have never discovered — we&#39;ll turn the enemy team&#39;s mentality straight to &amp;quot;wheelchair factory settings.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Hidden Rhythm of AK Spray Control: The &#39;Don&#39;t Compensate for the First Two Shots&#39; Rule That 90% of Newbies Get Wrong</title>
      <link>https://acebase.cc/posts/the-hidden-rhythm-of-ak-spray-control-en/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 03 Jun 2026 10:00:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://acebase.cc/posts/the-hidden-rhythm-of-ak-spray-control-en/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;the-hidden-rhythm-of-ak-spray-control-the-dont-compensate-for-the-first-two-shots-rule-that-90-of-newbies-get-wrong&#34;&gt;The Hidden Rhythm of AK Spray Control: The &amp;quot;Don&#39;t Compensate for the First Two Shots&amp;quot; Rule That 90% of Newbies Get Wrong&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Introduction:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Do you think that because the AK has high recoil, you should yank your mouse down as soon as you start firing? Wrong! The video immediately debunks a widespread misconception – 90% of newbies are &amp;quot;pulling down uselessly.&amp;quot; The real secret of high-level players lies in the milliseconds between bullets leaving the barrel: the first two bullets are nearly on top of each other, and only the third starts to jump up. Mastering this physical rule, combined with the micro-adjustment of &amp;quot;slightly twisting your mouse right,&amp;quot; allows you to make the AK spray with the precision of a 3-round burst. This article will break down the complete spray control rhythm chain from 3 to 15 bullets and tell you why &amp;quot;letting go&amp;quot; is more critical than &amp;quot;holding down.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>AK vs Galil: The Most Heartbreaking Economic Paradox in CS2</title>
      <link>https://acebase.cc/posts/ak-vs-galil-the-most-heartbreaking-economic-paradox-in-cs2-en/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 02 Jun 2026 12:11:56 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://acebase.cc/posts/ak-vs-galil-the-most-heartbreaking-economic-paradox-in-cs2-en/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;ak-vs-galil-the-most-heartbreaking-economic-paradox-in-cs2--its-not-that-you-cant-win-its-that-you-cant-afford-full-armor-but-still-insist-on-buying-the-ak&#34;&gt;AK vs Galil: The Most Heartbreaking Economic Paradox in CS2 — It&#39;s Not That You Can&#39;t Win, It&#39;s That You Can&#39;t Afford Full Armor But Still Insist on Buying the AK&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Introduction:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;In &lt;em&gt;CS2&lt;/em&gt; Terrorist rounds, what really makes your blood pressure spike isn&#39;t getting headshot — it&#39;s staring at that &amp;quot;$2300&amp;quot; in the bottom right corner, agonizing: should I buy the AK or the Galil? You can afford the gun but not the armor, or you can afford the armor but it empties your wallet for smokes and flashes? This video uses a witty yet sharp approach to expose the &amp;quot;cost-performance trap&amp;quot; that new and intermediate players most often fall into. It doesn&#39;t talk about mystical spray control; it just calculates a clear economic + damage + margin-for-error account — it turns out, what you lack isn&#39;t feel, but a &amp;quot;sensible&amp;quot; rifle.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
